   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi there,<div><br></div><div>You should be able to change the size of the parameters by adding  cex.lab = 2 (to double the size) to your call to &quot;scatter&quot;. Alternatively, you could extract the x values and y values using summary(pramx), and set up your own plot, where you might have more flexibility. </div><div><br></div><div>On a related note, I was reading help file for the package and discovered they have a function called &quot;showmekittens&quot; It does exactly what you would expect.</div></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_attr\">On Mon, Dec 9, 2019 at 6:24 AM mladen cucak &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">mlade...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div></div>"
    ],
